2:T457,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Workplace Conflict De-Escalation: The PAUSE Protocol & Clarity Frame (2026 Guide)","description":"Learn how to de-escalate workplace conflict in 90 seconds using the PAUSE Protocol, the Clarity Frame, and somatic nervous system regulation for managers and executives.","datePublished":"2026-11-22","dateModified":"2026-11-24","articleSection":"Business & Workplace","keywords":"workplace conflict de-escalation, PAUSE protocol leadership, how to de-escalate a tense meeting, executive emotional regulation, clarity frame communication, psychological safety in the workplace, nervous system regulation at work","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vibehyr.com/blog/workplace-de-escalation-pause-protocol-clarity-frame"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Keisha Solomon","jobTitle":"Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe Hyr","url":"https://vibehyr.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vibehyr.com/icons/icon-512.png"}},"image":"https://vibehyr.com/images/og-image.png"}3:T55b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the fastest way to de-escalate conflict in a workplace meeting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The fastest way to de-escalate a tense meeting is to interrupt the automatic defensive reflex using a 3-second physiological pause, drop your vocal speed to 80% of normal pace, and apply the Clarity Frame: restate the shared objective behind the other person's frustration without absorbing their hostility."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does defending yourself in a meeting make conflict worse?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When someone challenges you at Stage 2 of the Conflict Escalation Ladder and you respond with rapid self-justification, their amygdala interprets your defense as counter-aggression. Slowing down and validating the core operational concern removes the friction their nervous system is pushing against."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the PAUSE Protocol in workplace leadership?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PAUSE stands for Pause (3-second breath), Acknowledge (name the shared stake without blame), Understand (translate emotion into an operational priority via the Clarity Frame), Select (choose an intentional response aligned with outcomes), and Engage (commit to one clear next action)."}}]}8:["slug","workplace-de-escalation-pause-protocol-clarity-frame","d"]
